From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:59:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] [ROCm][Inkling2] NVFP4 and MXFP8 routed experts on RDNA4
 (gfx12)

Original AEON work (clean room, from docs/inkling2-rocm/SPEC.md).
RDNA4 has no FP4 MMA and the upstream MXFP8 path needs gfx950
tl.dot_scaled, so experts are served from the checkpoint packed weights
with in-register decode to bf16 and bf16 WMMA:

- ops/moe_dequant.py: bit-exact E2M1/E4M3/E8M0 decoders, grouped expert
  GEMM with fused softcapped SwiGLU (reference rounding: bf16 GEMM out,
  fp32 activation, bf16), row gather by sorted routing, deterministic
  fp32 top-k combine. Host-sync free tile planning.
- moe_gfx12.py: fp32 sigmoid router with score-correction bias and
  route_scale, expert params named like upstream nvidia/moe.py, EP = TP
  sharding. w13 gate/up rows are de-interleaved once at load (the
  checkpoint interleaves them, as the transformers converter documents).

Signed-off-by: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
